# Paths graphify must not pull into the code knowledge graph.
#
# .githooks/ holds shell scripts carrying a #!/bin/sh shebang, so graphify
# classifies them as code and graphs them. They are tooling that operates on the
# project rather than part of it, and scripts/graph-build.mjs refuses to publish
# a graph containing anything outside app/, work/ and scripts/ - so without this
# line every build fails its own scope check.
#
# Everything else out of scope (node_modules, app/data, backups, graphify-out)
# is already covered by .gitignore, which graphify honours by default.
.githooks/
